examples.jsonl contains code excerpts from the godot-rust project (https://github.com/godot-rust):
the book, demo-projects and gdext's integration tests. They are licensed under the Mozilla Public
License 2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/). Each entry's "src" field names the file it came from.
Rebuild with training/build_examples.py.

Entries whose "src" starts with "github" come from open-source projects found by
training/crawl_github.py. Only permissively licensed repos are used, and the license is named in
each entry's "src". Entries marked "ember-verified" are RusticEngine's own training examples.

Blender Manual excerpts (design.jsonl entries with "kind": "manual")
  The Blender Manual by the Blender Documentation Team (https://projects.blender.org/blender/documentation),
  https://docs.blender.org/manual/, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
  Text was converted from reStructuredText and shortened; each entry links its source page.
